DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(qw(
    PGstandard.pl
    PGML.pl
    parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl
    PGcourse.pl
));
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

Context('Matrix');
$A = Matrix([
    [ non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1), non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1) ],
    [ non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1), non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1) ],
]);
$B = Matrix([
    [ non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1), non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1) ],
    [ non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1), non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1) ],
    [ non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1), non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1) ],
]);
$C = Matrix([
    [ non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1), non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1) ],
    [ non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1), non_zero_random(-5, 5, 1) ],
]);

$k1   = random(2, 7, 1);
$k2   = random(2, 7, 1);
$ans1 = -$k1 * $B;
$ans2 = $k1 * $A - $k2 * $C;

$ma1 = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ["The scalar product \(-$k1 B\) does not exist."],
        [ "The scalar product \(-$k1 B\) is %s*.", $ans1->copy ],
        [ "The scalar product \(-$k1 B\) is %s*.", $ans2->copy ]
    ],
    1,
    labels => [ 'I', 'II', 'III' ]
);
$ma2 = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ["The matrix sum \(A + B\) does not exist."],
        [ "The matrix sum \(A + B\) is %s*.", $ans1->copy ],
        [ "The matrix sum \(A + B\) is %s*.", $ans2->copy ]
    ],
    0,
    labels => [ 'I', 'II', 'III' ]
);
$ma3 = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ["The linear combination \($k1 A - $k2 C\;\) does not exist."],
        [ "The linear combination \($k1 A - $k2 C\;\) is %s*.", $ans1->copy ],
        [ "The linear combination \($k1 A - $k2 C\;\) is %s*.", $ans2->copy ]
    ],
    2,
    labels => [ 'I', 'II', 'III' ]
);

BEGIN_PGML
Consider the three matrices:

        [``A=[$A]``], [``B=[$B]``], and [``C=[$C]``]

For each of the following matrix operations,
determine if the operation is defined or not. If the
operation is defined, select the appropriate form,
then enter in the answer.

a) Compute the scalar product [``-[$k1]B``]:

        [_]*{$ma1}

b) Compute the matrix sum [``A + B``]:

        [_]*{$ma2}

c) Compute the linear combination [``[$k1]A - [$k2]C\;``]:

        [_]*{$ma3}

END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
